# Cursor rule — ADR-048 multi-lang documentation bar

[Corpus: adr/ADR-048] [Corpus: docstrings]

## Must

- When editing product `packages/*/src`, `apps/backend`, `apps/worker`, `apps/frontend`,
  shipping `apps/e2e` helpers, or `packages/*/rust/src`: keep NumPy / TSDoc / rustdoc at the
  ADR-048 bar (public Examples / executable `@example` / runnable Rust `# Examples`).
- Prefer make targets: `check-docs`, `test-doctest`, `check-docs-ts` (presence **and**
  executable `@example` harness), `check-docs-rust` (pure-Rust `cargo test --doc`, no
  Python interpreter required for examples).
- Treat warnings and infos as failures for monorepo quality gates; do not add suppressions.
- Cite `[Corpus: docstrings]` / `[Corpus: adr/ADR-048]` in agent/docs commits — never in
  operator-facing OpenAPI/UI copy.

## Must not

- Introduce undocumented public or private product symbols in in-scope trees.
- Use Rust `pub` exemption globs to skip `# Examples`, or require Python to run Rust doctests.
- Change convert/validate/decode/disseminate wire behavior or pack-engine shapes to “pass”
  documentation work.
- Cite EV-/ADR-/TC- ids in operator-visible strings.
